       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 30 mg is three times the maximum recommended daily dose of 10 mg. The usual range is 2.5 to 10 mg once daily. At 30 mg the risks include severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Overdose can also cause prolonged shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nCould you confirm which of these you intended?\n\n- **10 mg once daily**, the standard maximum.\n- **5 mg once daily**, a common starting dose, or another dose within the 2.5 to 10 mg range.\n- **30 mg is intended.** If so, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed the dose.\n\nIf the 30 mg was a typo or a different drug or dose was meant, tell me the correction and I'll enter it right away."
